The Ford F-three-fifty is sixth at fifteen

280
00:11:34,575 --> 00:11:37,103
point one, and the F-one-fifty is not

281
00:11:37,103 --> 00:11:38,811
in the top twelve either.

282
00:11:38,991 --> 00:11:40,614
So for both companies,

283
00:11:40,614 --> 00:11:43,419
the heavy-duty truck is more likely to

284
00:11:43,419 --> 00:11:46,444
go the distance than its half-ton cousin.

285
00:11:46,794 --> 00:11:48,049
And on sales,

286
00:11:48,049 --> 00:11:49,883
the opposite holds.

287
00:11:50,063 --> 00:11:53,640
The Ford F-Series sold five hundred fifty-seven

288
00:11:53,640 --> 00:11:55,848
thousand through nine months,

289
00:11:55,848 --> 00:11:59,121
and the Silverado one thousand five hundred

290
00:11:59,121 --> 00:12:02,395
and two thousand five hundred together sold

291
00:12:02,395 --> 00:12:04,831
more than four hundred thousand.

292
00:12:05,011 --> 00:12:06,891
The half-tons dominate.

293
00:12:07,071 --> 00:12:09,411
So the market buys the truck that

294
00:12:09,411 --> 00:12:11,041
is easier to live with,

295
00:12:11,041 --> 00:12:13,451
and the truck that holds its value

296
00:12:13,451 --> 00:12:15,790
best is the one fewer people buy.

297
00:12:15,970 --> 00:12:17,739
That is a very old pattern in

298
00:12:17,739 --> 00:12:18,898
the truck business,

299
00:12:18,898 --> 00:12:20,545
and the numbers confirm it.

300
00:12:20,894 --> 00:12:22,531
So which should you buy?

301
00:12:22,711 --> 00:12:24,954
If you tow or haul heavy loads,

302
00:12:24,954 --> 00:12:27,919
every week, the heavy-duty truck is built

303
00:12:27,919 --> 00:12:30,306
for it, and the numbers on resale

304
00:12:30,306 --> 00:12:32,475
and longevity are on its side.

305
00:12:32,655 --> 00:12:35,005
If you use a truck mostly for

306
00:12:35,005 --> 00:12:37,192
commuting and family trips,

307
00:12:37,192 --> 00:12:39,379
with an occasional trailer,

308
00:12:39,379 --> 00:12:41,809
a half-ton is easier to drive,

309
00:12:41,809 --> 00:12:43,267
and often cheaper.

310
00:12:43,447 --> 00:12:46,223
The mistake is to buy the heavy-duty

311
00:12:46,223 --> 00:12:47,765
truck for the image,

312
00:12:47,765 --> 00:12:50,155
or to buy the half-ton and push

313
00:12:50,155 --> 00:12:52,700
it past its limits every weekend.

314
00:12:53,050 --> 00:12:55,487
There is one more thing to consider,

315
00:12:55,487 --> 00:12:57,044
and it is about timing.

316
00:12:57,224 --> 00:13:00,194
A heavy-duty truck costs more to buy,

317
00:13:00,194 --> 00:13:02,843
and the numbers say that it loses

318
00:13:02,843 --> 00:13:03,726
less value.

319
00:13:03,906 --> 00:13:06,430
That means the money you pay at

320
00:13:06,430 --> 00:13:09,199
the start comes back more fully at

321
00:13:09,199 --> 00:13:09,850
the end.

322
00:13:10,030 --> 00:13:11,062
For a business,

323
00:13:11,062 --> 00:13:13,678
that matters, because the truck can be

324
00:13:13,678 --> 00:13:15,742
an asset on the balance sheet.

325
00:13:15,922 --> 00:13:17,318
For a private buyer,

326
00:13:17,318 --> 00:13:18,643
it may matter less,

327
00:13:18,643 --> 00:13:20,737
because the cash you tie up in

328
00:13:20,737 --> 00:13:23,179
the truck cannot be used elsewhere.

329
00:13:23,528 --> 00:13:26,276
Finally, a word about the numbers in

330
00:13:26,276 --> 00:13:27,116
this video.

331
00:13:27,296 --> 00:13:30,030
Most of them are estimates or reported

332
00:13:30,030 --> 00:13:31,973
figures from third parties,

333
00:13:31,973 --> 00:13:34,492
and they were collected in the fall

334
00:13:34,492 --> 00:13:36,003
of twenty twenty-six.

335
00:13:36,183 --> 00:13:39,576
Sales tables are reasonably precise,

336
00:13:39,576 --> 00:13:44,099
but resale and longevity numbers are statistical

337
00:13:44,099 --> 00:13:45,042
estimates.

338
00:13:45,222 --> 00:13:47,332
Use them to narrow the list,

339
00:13:47,332 --> 00:13:49,668
and then check the exact truck.

340
00:13:49,848 --> 00:13:52,757
The best information about a used truck

341
00:13:52,757 --> 00:13:55,367
is its service record and a careful

342
00:13:55,367 --> 00:13:56,187
inspection.

343
00:13:56,537 --> 00:13:58,697
So what is the final twist?

344
00:13:58,877 --> 00:14:01,298
It is about why heavy-duty trucks are

345
00:14:01,298 --> 00:14:02,411
falling in sales,

346
00:14:02,411 --> 00:14:04,439
and the sources we found do not

347
00:14:04,439 --> 00:14:05,355
give a reason.

348
00:14:05,535 --> 00:14:07,599
We can offer what the numbers do

349
00:14:07,599 --> 00:14:07,857
say.

350
00:14:08,037 --> 00:14:10,489
The price of trucks has risen,

351
00:14:10,489 --> 00:14:14,248
the full-size average is sixty-seven thousand,

352
00:14:14,248 --> 00:14:16,782
four hundred forty-six dollars,

353
00:14:16,782 --> 00:14:20,622
and heavy-duty trucks are more expensive still.

354
00:14:20,802 --> 00:14:23,101
The market for work trucks may be

355
00:14:23,101 --> 00:14:24,773
more sensitive to price,

356
00:14:24,773 --> 00:14:26,097
and to the economy,

357
00:14:26,097 --> 00:14:28,465
than the market for family trucks.

358
00:14:28,645 --> 00:14:30,814
But that is an interpretation,

359
00:14:30,814 --> 00:14:31,826
not a finding.

360
00:14:32,176 --> 00:14:34,498
What the numbers do show is that

361
00:14:34,498 --> 00:14:37,546
the heavy-duty trucks are a very different

362
00:14:37,546 --> 00:14:37,981
asset.

363
00:14:38,161 --> 00:14:41,519
They lose about twenty to twenty-five percent

364
00:14:41,519 --> 00:14:42,564
in five years,

365
00:14:42,564 --> 00:14:46,071
compared with thirty-eight to forty percent for

366
00:14:46,071 --> 00:14:46,892
a half-ton.

367
00:14:47,072 --> 00:14:49,521
Take an example of a truck that

368
00:14:49,521 --> 00:14:52,285
costs seventy thousand dollars new.

369
00:14:52,465 --> 00:14:54,766
At the Ram's or the Ford's rate,

370
00:14:54,766 --> 00:14:57,067
that is a loss of about fourteen

371
00:14:57,067 --> 00:14:59,872
thousand to seventeen thousand dollars.

372
00:15:00,052 --> 00:15:01,899
At the F-one-fifty's rate,

373
00:15:01,899 --> 00:15:04,313
it is about twenty-seven thousand.

374
00:15:04,493 --> 00:15:06,598
A work truck can be a better

375
00:15:06,598 --> 00:15:09,230
store of value than a family truck.

376
00:15:09,579 --> 00:15:12,027
But a store of value is only

377
00:15:12,027 --> 00:15:14,038
useful if you can sell.

378
00:15:14,218 --> 00:15:16,814
In a market where the heavy-duty lines

379
00:15:16,814 --> 00:15:19,342
are shrinking, there may be fewer new

380
00:15:19,342 --> 00:15:20,981
trucks and fewer buyers,

381
00:15:20,981 --> 00:15:23,099
and that is something to watch.

382
00:15:23,279 --> 00:15:25,259
We do not have used price data

383
00:15:25,259 --> 00:15:26,844
in the sources we found.

384
00:15:27,024 --> 00:15:30,157
A careful buyer checks local prices for

385
00:15:30,157 --> 00:15:31,442
the exact truck,

386
00:15:31,442 --> 00:15:34,736
and compares the five-year picture to the

387
00:15:34,736 --> 00:15:36,986
cost of a lease or a rental,

388
00:15:36,986 --> 00:15:39,075
if the work is occasional.

389
00:15:39,424 --> 00:15:41,551
So what should you check before you

390
00:15:41,551 --> 00:15:44,347
buy a heavy-duty truck in twenty twenty-seven?

391
00:15:44,527 --> 00:15:47,311
First, whether you really need one,

392
00:15:47,311 --> 00:15:49,856
because a half-ton can do a lot.

393
00:15:50,036 --> 00:15:52,591
Second, the exact configuration,

394
00:15:52,591 --> 00:15:54,268
the engine, the axle,

395
00:15:54,268 --> 00:15:57,142
the payload and the towing figure on

396
00:15:57,142 --> 00:15:58,500
the door sticker.

397
00:15:58,680 --> 00:16:02,195
Third, the five-year resale value for that

398
00:16:02,195 --> 00:16:02,697
model.

399
00:16:02,877 --> 00:16:05,749
And fourth, whether the model is still

400
00:16:05,749 --> 00:16:09,678
being built, because the Silverado medium-duty shows

401
00:16:09,678 --> 00:16:10,888
that it can end.

402
00:16:11,237 --> 00:16:13,080
We put all of this into a

403
00:16:13,080 --> 00:16:17,135
checklist, the Twenty Twenty-Seven Truck Buyer's Guide.

404
00:16:17,315 --> 00:16:19,478
It covers the numbers to check,

405
00:16:19,478 --> 00:16:21,572
the questions to ask a dealer,

406
00:16:21,572 --> 00:16:24,363
and the warning signs we walked through.

407
00:16:24,543 --> 00:16:26,869
The link is in the description and

408
00:16:26,869 --> 00:16:28,374
in the pinned comment.

409
00:16:28,554 --> 00:16:31,220
If you want to know which engines

410
00:16:31,220 --> 00:16:33,240
to avoid in a used truck,

411
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:36,391
subscribe, because that is coming soon.

412
00:16:36,571 --> 00:16:37,824
Thanks for watching.
